From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VIctory contributor <contributor@users.noreply.invalid>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 23:24:19 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Host heap: a made slot is found without the slots' lock
 and kept resources sit behind 64 locks (VICTORY_HEAP_LOCKS=1|alt, off by
 default)

Hand port of the VICTORY_HEAP_LOCKS half of fork commit 5d659e0c8 (after fork
pull request #1146 part 1) onto b47. The other half of that commit
(VICTORY_TABLE_STAGES, draw.rs) is not needed for it and is left out, as are
the fork's lock-wait counters, which this line does not have.

With the switch: HostHeap::mirror answers from an atomic for a slot already
made from the record its draw names (0 while a slot is made again, set after
it is kept), and HostHeap::keep holds only its slot's piece of `kept` and
lets the old resource go outside the lock. Without it: every keep stands in
one line (kept_one) as before.

(cherry picked by hand from 5d659e0c8)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
